fix: restore the page slice guards and bound the page from its old end

Slicing both halves unconditionally panicked whenever the page did not
start at the oldest available pair: an empty journal half sliced
`start..0`, and a page ending below the journal total underflowed
`current_to - journal_total`. Both halves now take a non-empty range or
an empty slice, and a test covers the case that was missing — a journal
backed transcript with a non-zero offset.

The whole-page bound now drops the *oldest* pairs of the requested range
instead of the newest: `offset` counts from the newest end, so it is the
knob the omission note points at, and it has to reach what was omitted.
The header reports the range actually rendered. Constant docs say bytes
(2000 / 32 000) rather than KB, matching what the code compares against.